   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "נָפַל עָלָיו גַּל וְכוּ׳. קָא סָלְקָא דַּעְתָּךְ דְּאִי בָּעֵי מָצֵי שָׁקֵיל לֵיהּ.",
   "en": "The mishna continues: If «a pile» of stones «fell on» the eiruv prior to the onset of Shabbat, it is not a valid eiruv. «It» might «enter your mind» to say that the mishna is referring to a case «where if one wanted he could take» the eiruv, i.e., where it is physically possible to clear the stones and remove the eiruv from underneath them. The only reason he cannot do so is because of the rabbinic prohibition to handle items that are set-aside, such as stones, on Shabbat."
  }
